# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three nested repositories.
#
# This workspace holds three Git repositories and is itself a fourth. Without
# these rules Git sees the nested repos and offers to add them as broken
# submodule-like entries whose contents it will not track. They are public and
# manage themselves; see the README for links.
#
# This block is the one prescribed by docs/1-local-full-infra-guide.md, in
# "A note on nesting Git repos".
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
lfi-service-1-app/
lfi-service-2-app/
lfi-infrastructure-gitops/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only working material. Build-process artifacts and tool state, not
# follower-facing content.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.superpowers/
.tmp/
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/
diagrams/
tmp.txt

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Nothing here should ever exist at the workspace root, but the rules
# are cheap and the failure mode is permanent.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
token.json
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes from agent sessions. These have contained work email addresses,
# internal hostnames, and credential assessments. They must never be published.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
HANDOFF-*.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/ is an allowlist, not a blocklist.
#
# Agent sessions write planning documents into docs/, and at least one of those
# has contained internal hostnames and personal addresses. A blocklist would
# need updating every time a new one lands, and forgetting once is permanent.
# So: ignore everything in docs/, then name the files that are meant to ship.
#
# Adding a genuine new doc means adding a matching negation here. That is the
# intended friction.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/*
!docs/1-local-full-infra-guide.md
!docs/2-multi-env-infra-guide.md
!docs/resource_check.md
!docs/resource_check.sh

# Same reasoning for the trackers at the root.
tracker_*.md
!tracker_1_local_infra.md
!tracker_2_multi_env.md
